# postcss (CVE-2026-45623, GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849) and postcss's own bundled nanoid (CVE-2026-67213)
# — REAL, PRODUCTION, NOT install-time-only: `pnpm why` confirms postcss 8.4.31 and nanoid 3.3.16
# are bundled INSIDE next@14.2.35 itself (Next's own built-in CSS pipeline), not independent,
# independently-bumpable dependencies — the devDependency-only postcss instance (via vite/
# autoprefixer) is already on a patched 8.5.17 and is not flagged at all. Every one of these CVEs
# traces to exactly one real root cause: apps/web/package.json pins `"next": "^14.2.15"`, and every
# available fix is on Next 15.x/16.x — a MAJOR framework version upgrade (App Router/middleware/
# server-action behavior changes) that needs its own dedicated task with real regression testing,
# not a same-pass drive-by bump alongside a CI-workflow fix. Flagged explicitly to the Product
# Owner, not silently accepted.
CVE-2026-44573
CVE-2026-44578
CVE-2026-64641
CVE-2026-64645
CVE-2026-64649
GHSA-8h8q-6873-q5fj
GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf
GHSA-q4gf-8mx6-v5v3
